  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform rod <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is suspended from a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>, at a variable distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>, as shown. To make the rod horizontal, a mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is suspended from its end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. A set of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> value is recorded. The appropriate variables that give a straight line, when plotted, are:<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/df5930d6-7cc5-4b0f-a245-0f50a68cb593-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 159px;\" />",
